+# Switch 2 titles (experimental)
+
+Switch 2 support comes from Takoroka's **eden-nx2** (<https://git.eden-emu.dev/Takoroka/eden-nx2>,
+branch `eden-nx2`, GPL-3.0-or-later like Eden), a fork of Eden master that boots Switch 2 titles on
+PC; its findings are in that tree's `NX2_NOTES.md` and `NX2_GPU_THREAD_SPLIT.md`. The port to the
+PS5 follows **Oliv3rmoon's Nightshade** (<https://github.com/Oliv3rmoon/Nightshade>, branch
+`feature/nx2`, `docs/NX2_PORT.md` there), whose first commits are this fork's ancestors: its pin
+move, session settings, per-session reset and Switch 2 only optimizations are taken from it, onto
+this fork's own derivations.
+
+Nothing here has run on a console: nobody here has a Switch 2 dump. Expect crashes, missing graphics
+and low frame rates.
+
+## The pin
+
+Eden is eden-nx2 at `50fa86bbbc403ad565eb44fcc281f16f77c69e15` (Eden master at `26a03d2473`, then
+eden-nx2's commits), the archive git.eden-emu.dev makes of it, checked by sha256 in
+`tools/deps.json` and `UPSTREAM.json` (Nightshade's, the same on two downloads). The same commit is
+on GitHub in Djihads80/Eglantine's `nx2` branch, for reading it where git.eden-emu.dev is out of
+reach. If the archive's sha256 ever stops matching (Forgejo builds archives on request), compare the
+unpacked tree with `git archive` of the commit and pin the new hash.
+
+What moved with it:
+
+- `tools/eden-patches/01` to `04` apply to eden-nx2 as they are (rebased, context only); `12` is new:
+  two optimizations eden-nx2 measured only with Switch 2 titles (same-value 3D register writes
+  dropped, inline uploads' cache invalidation deferred) wait for a Switch 2 driver
+  (`Tegra::g_nx2_ampere`), so Switch 1 games keep Eden's behaviour.
+- Every derivation in `headless/CMakeLists.txt` and `tools/prepare-vulkan-port.py` still finds its
+  anchor. Changed for eden-nx2: the guest core's idle wait (its flag is a `std::atomic<bool>`; this
+  fork's spin-then-sleep replaces eden-nx2's optional poll), `KSpinLock` (eden-nx2's own
+  spin-then-wait lock, spinning `kernel_spin_iterations`), `vfs_real.cpp`'s open file cap (a
+  function now), the image allocator's retry outside the budget (eden-nx2 retries itself; it is
+  counted and reported as before), the split GPU thread stopped with the worker.
+- Dropped because upstream does it now: `GetPseudoDeviceId` without control data (seeded from the
+  program ID), and the `texture_cache/util.h` small-vector workaround.
+- **Six emulated cores.** eden-nx2 raises `Core::Hardware::NUM_CPU_CORES` from 4 to 6 for every
+  title (Switch 1 titles leave 4 and 5 idle). Everything `headless/performance.h` counts per core is
+  sized by `kGuestCores` (6), and the derived `physical_core.cpp` asserts it: with four places, the
+  JIT callbacks, CPU write statistics and CPU samples of cores 4 and 5 were written past their arrays.
+- ASTC transcoding keeps half the hardware threads (eden-nx2 takes a quarter, measured on a PC).
+
+## Playing one
+
+- **Format.** eden-nx2 boots a Switch 2 title as a loose ExeFS (`exefs/main`, `main.npdm`, `rtld`,
+  `sdk`, `subsdk*`) with its RomFS in a sibling `romfs/`; it has no Switch 2 NSP or XCI support. Such
+  a game is a game folder holding `exefs/` and `romfs/`, and goes by the path of its main,
+  `<folder>/exefs/main` (`headless/exefs_game.h`). A Switch 1 game dumped the same way plays too.
+- **Title ID and detection.** The program ID in `main.npdm` (`eden_game_title_id`); a Switch 2 title
+  is one whose npdm has the Switch 2 layout (`eden_game_is_switch2`, eden-nx2's
+  `ProgramMetadata::IsSwitch2`). Its name is the folder's, or a `control.nacp` beside `exefs/`.
+- **Keys and firmware**: the user's own, as for any game. A loose ExeFS is already decrypted.
+- **A session** (`headless/main.cpp`): the 12 GiB memory layout, Eden's lowest GPU accuracy, no
+  reactive flushing, ASTC decoded on the GPU, eden-nx2's split GPU thread; `"switch2"` in the
+  settings file changes three of them (docs/SETTINGS.md). eden-nx2's Turing macro compiler stays off
+  (`EDEN_NX2_MME_JIT=0`): the console refuses the executable memory it asks for. eden-nx2's
+  process-wide Switch 2 state is put back before every session (`headless/nx2_session.h`), since this
+  program plays one game after another; the split GPU thread's mode is read once per session.
+
+## Risks on the PS5
+
+- **Memory.** The 12 GiB layout plus eden-nx2's 8 GiB for the graphics server is 20 GiB of guest
+  memory against about 12.4 GiB on the console: it works only while a title touches less than what
+  is left, guest memory being backed where it is written.
+- **CPU.** Six emulated cores and a second GPU thread on the console's Zen 2: expect CPU-bound frame
+  rates. `"switch2": { "gpu_split": false }` gives a core back.
+- **Sparse images.** Images over 2^28 texels become sparse images with nothing bound; without sparse
+  residency in the console's RADV they fail.
+
+## Checked here
+
+- The derivations run against eden-nx2 with every anchor found, in the PS5 build (with its graphics)
+  and the Linux host build, and every line they add on the old pin is added on eden-nx2 too or
+  explained above.
+- `headless/metadata_bridge.cpp`, `main.cpp` and `performance.cpp` compile against eden-nx2's
+  headers; the settings store's check (`preferences_check.cpp`) passes with the Switch 2 settings
+  and paths.
+- Not built for the console, and not run on one.
